The force–mass–acceleration relation is  

\[
F = m a \quad\Longrightarrow\quad a = \frac{F}{m}.
\]

Jen uses the same force \(F\) as Jack.  
Hence

\[
\frac{a_{\text{Jen}}}{a_{\text{Jack}}}
   = \frac{F/m_{\text{Jen}}}{F/m_{\text{Jack}}}
   = \frac{m_{\text{Jack}}}{m_{\text{Jen}}}
   = \frac{150\ \text{g}}{200\ \text{g}}
   = \frac{150}{200}
   = \frac{3}{4}.
\]

The fraction is already in lowest terms.

\[
\boxed{\frac{3}{4}}
\]

